================================================================================
ROUND 2 — CI rejected the inline form; declaration moved to the stylesheet
================================================================================

PR #3264 opened. 20 of 21 checks green; `validate-pr` FAILED with exit 50:

    REJECTED: CSP pattern hit in an added line :: /\.style\b/
      .style

The CSP gate (VTID-03714) scans lines `git diff` reports as ADDED on the
browser-served surface. The fix edited the `_root.style.cssText = ...` line, so
that line came through as added and matched `/\.style\b/`. Not a false positive
on untouched content — the rule (ALWAYS 36 / NEVER 24, no inline CSS) genuinely
bites this edit.

Resolution: move the declaration into the `.vtorb-overlay` rule in
`_injectStyles()`, which is the class `_renderOverlay()` already assigns to
`_root`, and revert the inline string to its original bytes.

Equally effective, and not a workaround: what is blocked is INHERITANCE from
`document.body`, not a specificity contest on this element. The two rules match
different elements and never compete. It is also the better home — the
stylesheet already carries the overlay's box and appearance, and the inline
string only mirrors it.

$ node --check services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
PARSE OK

$ npx jest test/frontend/orb-overlay-pointer-events.test.ts
  ✓ declares pointer-events:auto on the overlay
  ✓ declares it on the rule that matches the ROOT, not an inner element
  ✓ keeps the declaration out of the inline cssText (CSP surface)
  ✓ keeps the close button wired unconditionally — it was never disabled
  ✓ does not gate the overlay on any guided-topic state
Tests: 5 passed, 5 total

