$ git diff origin/main -- 'services/gateway/src/frontend/' 'services/gateway/dist/frontend/' > csp_diff.txt
$ node scripts/ci/validator-path-guard.cjs --csp-added-lines csp_diff.txt
No CSP pattern hits in added lines.   exit=0

--- CSP gate, mutation check (the inline form must STILL be rejected) ---
$ printf '+++ b/.../orb-widget.js\n+    _root.style.cssText = "pointer-events:auto;";\n' > csp_mutant.txt
$ node scripts/ci/validator-path-guard.cjs --csp-added-lines csp_mutant.txt
REJECTED: CSP pattern hit in an added line :: /\.style\b/   exit=1

So the new test ("keeps the declaration out of the inline cssText") pins a real
shippability constraint, not a style preference. Recorded in outputs/csp-gate.txt.

--- Behavioural proof RE-RUN in the shipped form ---
The probe previously applied `pointer-events:auto` as an inline style. Rewritten
to apply it through a `.vtorb-overlay` stylesheet rule, exactly as
`_injectStyles()` writes it, so the evidence exercises what actually deploys.

